  below (or the "preferred-citation" entry). The concept DOI always resolves
  to the latest version.
title: >-
  Two Models That Agree Beat the Best of Them Alone: Parameter-Free Connected-Component Consensus That Beats the Baseline under the Official BraTS-2023 Metrics
abstract: >-
  Self-correction under the official BraTS-2023 metrics. Re-evaluated at
  300-epoch convergence on the full 5-fold cross-validation (n = 1196) under
  the complete official metric set. The Signed-Distance-Transform (SDT)
  auxiliary head is null on the official lesion-wise ranking metrics
  (Holm p = 1.0) and Dice-neutral; its only robust effect is a recall-oriented
  shift (higher sensitivity, lower specificity, the latter showing up as
  spurious connected components). A parameter-free connected-component
  consensus (DistMap vetoed by a second model — baseline or the Kervadec head)
  is the only configuration that significantly beats the baseline on the
  official ranking metrics (lesion-wise Dice +0.024, Holm p = 4.5e-16;
  lesion-wise HD95 -9.49 mm, Holm p = 5.7e-26), by removing ~41% of spurious
  lesions at negligible recall cost. The archive bundles the manuscript
  (FR + EN) and the full analysis material.
